# UI/UX Standards

The application must feel like a professional, production-grade SaaS product at every touchpoint.
Target: reviewers and school administrators should never feel the UI is basic, incomplete, or inconsistent.

## Design System

- UI library: **MUI v6** with enhanced custom theme (`apps/web/src/theme/theme.ts`)
- Icons: **@mui/icons-material v6** — every nav item, action button, and status must have an icon
- Light **and dark** color schemes (MUI `colorSchemes` + CSS variables); user toggles Light/Dark/System via `ColorModeToggle`
- Sidebar: `sidebar.*` palette tokens (light surface in light mode, near-black in dark), active item is a tinted pill
- Brand accents: `brandVars` from `theme/theme.ts` (blue→violet gradient, glass top bar, soft shadows)
- Input variant: **filled** across all forms (avoids label-clip issues)
- Font: Inter or Segoe UI — clean, modern, legible

## Theme Tokens (use these, do not hardcode colors)

- `primary.main`: brand blue — used for CTAs, links, active states
- `background.default`: light grey page background (`#f4f6fb`)
- `background.paper`: white cards/panels
- `text.primary`: near-black (`#0f172a`)
- `text.secondary`: muted slate (`#475569`)
- `divider`: soft grey border (`#e3e8f0`)
- Sidebar: `sidebar.main` / `sidebar.active` / `sidebar.activeText` tokens (scheme-aware)
- Print headers / auth backdrop navy: `brand.navy` (`#0f2044`)

## Form Standards

- Always use `variant="filled"` for all TextField, Select inputs
- Every required field must show `*` in the label
- Real-time inline validation on blur (not only on submit)
- Error messages must be specific — not "Invalid input", say "Employee code must be 2–32 lowercase characters"
- Autofill/browser prefill must not turn inputs dark — override `-webkit-autofill` in theme
- Group related fields into logical sections using `FormSection` component
- Action buttons: primary action right-aligned, secondary/cancel left-aligned
- Success confirmation must show after every create/update/delete action (Snackbar or Alert)

## Page layout shells (required for new pages)

- **List pages:** `ListPageShell` + module icon, filters in outlined `Paper`, `TableIconLink` for row “View” actions
- **Create/edit forms:** `FormPageShell` + `FormSection` blocks + `FormPageFooter` (Cancel text, Save contained)
- **Detail pages:** `DetailPageShell` with optional `meta` sidebar and `DetailFactRow` for facts
- **Destructive actions:** `ConfirmDialog` — never `window.confirm`
- **Mutations:** prefer `useAppSnackbar().showSuccess()` / `showError()` over one-off success Alerts

## Navigation / Sidebar

- Uses `sidebar.*` tokens so it follows light/dark mode
- Nav items have icons from `@mui/icons-material` — icon + label, no icon-only
- Active nav item: `sidebar.activeText` on a `sidebar.active` tinted pill with a short accent bar
- Nav is grouped by section with overline section headers
- Nav items are filtered by the user's actual permissions — never show a link the user cannot access
- Logo area: "CampusOps" bold, beside a gradient school-icon tile

## Page Structure

- Every page starts with a `PageHeader` (title + optional description + optional action buttons)
- PageHeader title has a relevant icon beside it
- Lists/tables use `AppTable` with column headers, pagination, search, filters
- Empty states use `EmptyState` with a relevant icon and descriptive text — never blank white space
- Loading states use MUI `Skeleton` for table rows and card grids — not a spinner-only
- Error states use `Alert severity="error"` with a retry button

## Status Indicators

- All status chips must use `StatusChip` component with semantic colors:
  - ACTIVE / APPROVED / COMPLETED / PUBLISHED → green
  - PENDING / IN_PROGRESS / ASSIGNED / DRAFT → amber/orange
  - INACTIVE / REJECTED / CLOSED / ARCHIVED → grey
  - CRITICAL / OFFBOARDED → red
- Every status chip has a small icon matching the status

## Images & Visual Assets

- School-themed contextual images on the public landing page (from open-license sources like Unsplash)
- Module-specific illustrations on empty states (complaints, visitors, events, etc.)
- School logo placeholder: default school icon (MUI `SchoolOutlined`) — replaced by org logo when uploaded
- All images have alt text

## Landing Page (Public)

- Professional hero: large heading, tagline, two CTAs (Register School / Sign In)
- Feature grid: 8 modules with icon, name, one-line description
- "How it works" section: 3 steps (Register → Onboard → Operate)
- Trust section: target school types (CBSE, ICSE, International)
- Clean footer with links

## Responsiveness

- Mobile-first: sidebar collapses to hamburger on `xs/sm`
- Tables become stacked labelled cards on phones (`AppTable` / `ResponsiveTable`); dialogs go edge-to-edge with a 12px gutter (theme)
- Forms stack vertically on mobile, side-by-side on `md+`
- Cards use `Grid2` with responsive column counts

## Prohibited Patterns

- Do NOT hardcode colors outside the theme — use `sx` palette paths, `theme.vars.palette.*` or `brandVars`; verify both light and dark
- Do NOT show raw UUIDs or technical error codes to users
- Do NOT leave blank white pages while loading — always show skeleton or spinner
- Do NOT use `window.alert()` or browser dialogs for confirmation — use MUI Dialog
- Do NOT mix `outlined` and `filled` input variants in the same form
- Do NOT create a new component if an existing one can be extended

Before creating a new UI pattern, search the existing codebase for a similar pattern and reuse it.
